<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Kirina</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1235</span> · Also known as Kirina</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Kirina was fought around c. 1235 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sundiata-keita">Sundiata Keita</a> and Sumanguru Kante, ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sosso-empire">Sosso</a> kingdom. Sundiata won, freeing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mande-peoples">Mande peoples</a> from Sosso domination. The victory is traditionally regarded as the foundation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali-empire">Mali Empire</a>.</p></div>
